            <div xml:id="d418">

                <pb facs="0404" n="339" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg339"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123H875/198: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-08T19:00:00+01:00">December 8, 1936—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 8—4:08 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>514. My 507, December 4, 7 p.m.<anchor n="99" xml:id="d418-f1"/> and previous. I
                    understand from the Minister of Foreign Affairs that there is some difficulty in
                    connection with the visa of Hughes passport by the Italian Embassy in that it
                    states that he is assigned “to the Legation at Addis Ababa” instead of “to Addis
                    Ababa” to which latter designation the Italian authorities agreed. As the
                    objection of the Foreign Office is solely to the use of the words “Legation at”
                    on the passport itself I sincerely hope that this matter may be satisfactorily
                    arranged.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
